IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vic-nouns`
IMPORT `vic-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `vic-part4-b-powers`

-- Part IV, continued: ss 45 to 59.
-- s 44 (time) and s 49 (service by post) are in vic-interpretation-time.l4; s 55(2)(b) (age) is there too.
-- The definitions that sit inside these sections (ss 46A(4), 51(2), 54(3), 55(1)(b), 57(6)) are written with their sections.
-- Where an unless-clause is met ("the contrary intention appears"), the function answers the question "does the rule's consequence follow?" with JUST FALSE.

§ `Part IV -- Provisions applicable to Acts and subordinate instruments (ss 45 to 59)`

§§ `s 45 Construction of "may" and "shall"`

DECLARE VicWordUsedInConferringAPower IS ONE OF
    VicMay
    VicShall
    VicAnyOtherWord

-- s 45(1): in this Act or any Act passed (or subordinate instrument made) on or after the commencement of this Act, the word "may" used in conferring a power means the power may be exercised, or not, at discretion.
-- src:1026 | (1) Where in this Act or any Act passed or subordinate instrument made on or after the commencement of this Act the word "may" is used in conferring a power, that word shall be construed as meaning that the power so conferred may be exercised, or not, at discretion.
@ref s 45(1) (src:1026)
GIVEN word IS A VicWordUsedInConferringAPower, isThisActOrPassedOrMadeOnOrAfterTheCommencement IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s45(1) the power may be exercised, or not, at discretion` MEANS
    IF word EQUALS VicMay AND isThisActOrPassedOrMadeOnOrAfterTheCommencement THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 45(2): the word "shall" used in conferring a power means the power must be exercised.
-- src:1027 | (2) Where in this Act or any Act passed or subordinate instrument made on or after the commencement of this Act the word "shall" is used in conferring a power, that word shall be construed as meaning that the power so conferred must be exercised.
@ref s 45(2) (src:1027)
GIVEN word IS A VicWordUsedInConferringAPower, isThisActOrPassedOrMadeOnOrAfterTheCommencement IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s45(2) the power must be exercised` MEANS
    IF word EQUALS VicShall AND isThisActOrPassedOrMadeOnOrAfterTheCommencement THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 45(3): the section has effect notwithstanding any rule of construction to the contrary, and any such rule is abrogated for this Act and for any Act passed (or subordinate instrument made) on or after the commencement.
-- src:1028 | (3) The provisions of this section shall have effect notwithstanding any rule of construction to the contrary and any such rule is hereby abrogated with respect to this Act and any Act passed or subordinate instrument made on or after the commencement of this Act.
@ref s 45(3) (src:1028)
GIVEN aRuleOfConstructionToTheContraryIsRelied IS A BOOLEAN, isThisActOrPassedOrMadeOnOrAfterTheCommencement IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s45(3) the rule of construction to the contrary applies` MEANS
    IF aRuleOfConstructionToTheContraryIsRelied AND isThisActOrPassedOrMadeOnOrAfterTheCommencement THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 46 References to the Sovereign`

-- s 46(1): a reference to the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of the Act or making of the instrument is, unless the contrary intention appears, a reference to the Sovereign for the time being.
-- src:1032 | (1) In an Act or subordinate instrument a reference to the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of the Act or making of the subordinate instrument shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be construed as a reference to the Sovereign for the time being.
@ref s 46(1) (src:1032)
GIVEN isAReferenceToTheSovereignReigningAtTheTimeOfPassingOrMaking IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s46(1) the reference is a reference to the Sovereign for the time being` MEANS
    IF isAReferenceToTheSovereignReigningAtTheTimeOfPassingOrMaking AND (NOT contraryIntentionAppears) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE VicSovereignForTheTimeBeing IS ONE OF
    VicTheSovereignIsTheQueen
    VicTheSovereignIsTheKing

-- s 46(2): unless the contrary intention appears, if the Sovereign for the time being is the Queen, "His Majesty" is read as "Her Majesty" and "the King" as "the Queen"; if the King, "Her Majesty" is read as "His Majesty" and "the Queen" as "the King".
-- src:1034 | (2) Unless the contrary intention appears, in an Act or a subordinate instrument—
-- src:1035 | (a) if the Sovereign for the time being is the Queen—
-- src:1036 | (i) a reference to "His Majesty" is to be construed as a reference to "Her Majesty"; and
-- src:1037 | (ii) a reference to "the King" is to be construed as a reference to "the Queen"; and
-- src:1038 | (b) if the Sovereign for the time being is the King—
-- src:1039 | (i) a reference to "Her Majesty" is to be construed as a reference to "His Majesty"; and
-- src:1040 | (ii) a reference to "the Queen" is to be construed as a reference to "the King".
@ref s 46(2) (src:1034-1040)
GIVEN sovereign IS A VicSovereignForTheTimeBeing, expression IS A STRING, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s46(2) the expression is construed as a reference to` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN NOTHING
        IF sovereign EQUALS VicTheSovereignIsTheQueen AND expression EQUALS "His Majesty" THEN JUST "Her Majesty"
        IF sovereign EQUALS VicTheSovereignIsTheQueen AND expression EQUALS "the King" THEN JUST "the Queen"
        IF sovereign EQUALS VicTheSovereignIsTheKing AND expression EQUALS "Her Majesty" THEN JUST "His Majesty"
        IF sovereign EQUALS VicTheSovereignIsTheKing AND expression EQUALS "the Queen" THEN JUST "the King"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 46A Construction of provisions relating to entities representing, or not representing, the Crown`

-- s 46A(1) to (3): where an Act or subordinate instrument provides that an entity represents the Crown, it has the status, privileges and immunities of the Crown;
-- where it provides that the entity does not represent the Crown, it does not; unless the contrary intention appears.
-- Where no provision of either kind is made, that does not of itself give rise to any implication either way.
-- The input is what the Act or instrument provides: JUST TRUE (the entity represents the Crown), JUST FALSE (the entity does not represent the Crown), or NOTHING (no provision of either kind).
-- src:1044 | (1) If, in an Act or subordinate instrument, it is provided that an entity represents the Crown, that entity has, for all purposes, the status, privileges and immunities of the Crown, unless the contrary intention appears.
-- src:1045 | (2) If, in an Act or subordinate instrument, it is provided that an entity does not represent the Crown, that entity does not have, for any purpose, the status, privileges and immunities of the Crown, unless the contrary intention appears.
-- src:1046 | (3) The fact that no provision of a kind referred to in subsection (1) or (2) is made by any Act or subordinate instrument with respect to a particular entity does not of itself give rise to any implication as to whether or not the entity has, or does not have, the status, privileges and immunities of the Crown for any purpose.
@ref s 46A(1) and s 46A(2) and s 46A(3) (src:1044-1046)
GIVEN whatTheActOrInstrumentProvidesAboutRepresentingTheCrown IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s46A the entity has the status, privileges and immunities of the Crown` MEANS
    CONSIDER whatTheActOrInstrumentProvidesAboutRepresentingTheCrown
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST representsTheCrown THEN (IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST representsTheCrown)

-- s 46A(4): in this section Crown includes the State.
-- src:1047 | (4) In this section Crown includes the State.
@ref s 46A(4) (src:1047)
GIVEN thing IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s46A(4) the thing is within the Crown as the section uses the word` MEANS
    IF thing EQUALS "the State" THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 47 Reference to officer in general terms`

-- s 47: a reference in general terms to a person holding or occupying a particular office or position is, unless the contrary intention appears, a reference to all persons who at any time hold, occupy, act in or perform the duties of that office or position for the time being.
-- src:1049 | 47 Reference to officer in general terms
-- src:1050 | In an Act or subordinate instrument a reference in general terms to a person holding or occupying a particular office or position shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be construed as a reference to all persons who at any time hold, occupy, act in or perform the duties of that office or position for the time being.
@ref s 47 (src:1049-1050)
GIVEN isAReferenceInGeneralTermsToAPersonHoldingOrOccupyingAnOffice IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN, person IS A VicPersonRelativeToAnOffice
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s47 the person is within the reference` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT isAReferenceInGeneralTermsToAPersonHoldingOrOccupyingAnOffice THEN JUST FALSE
        IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN JUST FALSE
        IF person EQUALS VicSomeoneElse THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 48 References to officers, localities etc.`

DECLARE VicKindOfReferenceS48 IS ONE OF
    VicReferenceToAnOfficerOrOffice                                  -- s 48(a)
    VicReferenceToALocalityJurisdictionOrOtherMatterOrThing          -- s 48(b)
    VicAnyOtherReference48

-- s 48: unless the contrary intention appears, a reference to an officer or office is a reference to such an officer or office in and for Victoria, and a reference to a locality, jurisdiction or other matter or thing is a reference to such a locality, jurisdiction or matter or thing in and of Victoria.
-- src:1054 | (a) a reference to an officer or office shall be construed as a reference to such an officer or office in and for Victoria; and
-- src:1055 | (b) a reference to a locality, jurisdiction or other matter or thing shall be construed as a reference to such locality, jurisdiction or other matter or thing in and of Victoria.
@ref s 48(a) and s 48(b) (src:1054-1055)
GIVEN kind IS A VicKindOfReferenceS48, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN, isInVictoria IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s48 the reference is a reference to the officer, office, locality, jurisdiction, matter or thing in and for or of Victoria` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF kind EQUALS VicAnyOtherReference48 THEN NOTHING
        IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST isInVictoria

§§ `s 50 Rules of court`

-- s 50: where an Act or subordinate instrument confers jurisdiction on a court or other tribunal (or extends or varies it), the authority with power to make rules or orders regulating practice and procedure may, unless the contrary intention appears, make such rules or orders (including about costs) as appear to the authority necessary for regulating the practice and procedure of the court or tribunal in the exercise of that jurisdiction.
-- src:1066 | 50 Rules of court
-- src:1067 | Where an Act or subordinate instrument confers any jurisdiction on a court or other tribunal or extends or varies the jurisdiction of a court or other tribunal, the authority having for the time being power to make rules or orders regulating the practice and procedure of that court or tribunal may, unless the contrary intention appears, make such rules or orders (including rules or orders with respect to costs) as appear to the authority to be necessary for regulating the practice and procedure of that court or tribunal in the exercise of the jurisdiction so conferred, extended or varied.
@ref s 50 (src:1066-1067)
GIVEN conferredExtendedOrVariedTheJurisdictionOfACourtOrTribunal IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN, appearsToTheAuthorityToBeNecessaryForRegulatingPracticeAndProcedure IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s50 the authority may make the rule or order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT conferredExtendedOrVariedTheJurisdictionOfACourtOrTribunal THEN JUST FALSE
        IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN JUST FALSE
        IF appearsToTheAuthorityToBeNecessaryForRegulatingPracticeAndProcedure THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 51 Provisions as to offences under two or more laws`

DECLARE VicKindOfLaw IS ONE OF
    VicAnActOrAProvisionOfAnAct                          -- s 51(2)(a)
    VicASubordinateInstrumentOrAProvisionOfOne           -- s 51(2)(b)
    VicCommonLaw                                         -- s 51(2)(c)
    VicSomethingThatIsNotALaw

-- s 51(2): in subsection (1) law means an Act or a provision of an Act, a subordinate instrument or a provision of one, or common law.
-- src:1071 | (2) In subsection (1) law means—
-- src:1072 | (a) an Act or a provision of an Act;
-- src:1073 | (b) a subordinate instrument or a provision of a subordinate instrument; or
-- src:1074 | (c) common law.
@ref s 51(2) (src:1071-1074)
GIVEN kind IS A VicKindOfLaw
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s51(2) the thing is a law` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN VicSomethingThatIsNotALaw THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 51(1): where an act or omission constitutes an offence under two or more laws, the offender shall, unless the contrary intention expressly appears, be liable to be prosecuted under either or any or all of those laws.
-- src:1070 | (1) Where an act or omission constitutes an offence under two or more laws, the offender shall, unless the contrary intention expressly appears, be liable to be prosecuted under either or any or all of those laws but shall not be liable to be punished more than once for the same act or omission.
@ref s 51(1) (src:1070)
GIVEN numberOfLawsUnderWhichTheActOrOmissionIsAnOffence IS A NUMBER, contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s51(1) the offender is liable to be prosecuted under any or all of those laws` MEANS
    IF numberOfLawsUnderWhichTheActOrOmissionIsAnOffence AT LEAST 2 AND (NOT contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 51(1): but the offender shall not, unless the contrary intention expressly appears, be liable to be punished more than once for the same act or omission.
-- src:1070 | (1) Where an act or omission constitutes an offence under two or more laws, the offender shall, unless the contrary intention expressly appears, be liable to be prosecuted under either or any or all of those laws but shall not be liable to be punished more than once for the same act or omission.
@ref s 51(1) (src:1070)
GIVEN numberOfLawsUnderWhichTheActOrOmissionIsAnOffence IS A NUMBER, contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s51(1) the offender is liable to be punished more than once for the same act or omission` MEANS
    IF numberOfLawsUnderWhichTheActOrOmissionIsAnOffence AT LEAST 2 AND (NOT contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears) THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 52 Summary proceedings`

-- s 52: if an Act or subordinate instrument authorises or requires a proceeding or matter to be heard and determined summarily or by or before the Magistrates' Court (a), uses other words implying that (b), or does not provide a form or mode of procedure for the hearing and determination (c),
-- then, unless the contrary intention appears, the proceeding or matter must be heard and determined only by or before the Magistrates' Court.
-- src:1079 | 52 Summary proceedings
-- src:1080 | If an Act or subordinate instrument—
-- src:1081 | (a) authorises or requires a proceeding or matter to be heard and determined—
-- src:1082 | (i) summarily; or
-- src:1083 | (ii) by or before the Magistrates' Court; or
-- src:1084 | (b) uses any other words that imply that a proceeding or matter is to be heard and determined by or before the Magistrates' Court; or
-- src:1085 | (c) does not provide a form or mode of procedure for the hearing and determination of a proceeding or matter—
-- src:1086 | then, unless the contrary intention appears, the proceeding or matter must be heard and determined only by or before the Magistrates' Court.
@ref s 52 (src:1079-1086)
GIVEN authorisesOrRequiresSummarilyOrByOrBeforeTheMagistratesCourt IS A BOOLEAN, usesOtherWordsImplyingTheMagistratesCourt IS A BOOLEAN, providesNoFormOrModeOfProcedure IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s52 the proceeding or matter must be heard and determined only by or before the Magistrates' Court` MEANS
    IF (authorisesOrRequiresSummarilyOrByOrBeforeTheMagistratesCourt OR usesOtherWordsImplyingTheMagistratesCourt OR providesNoFormOrModeOfProcedure) AND (NOT contraryIntentionAppears)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 53 Strict compliance with prescribed forms not necessary`

-- s 53: where a form is prescribed by an Act or subordinate instrument for any purpose, any form in or to the like effect of the prescribed form shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be sufficient in law.
-- src:1088 | 53 Strict compliance with prescribed forms not necessary
-- src:1089 | Where a form is prescribed by an Act or subordinate instrument for any purpose, any form in or to the like effect of the prescribed form shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be sufficient in law.
@ref s 53 (src:1088-1089)
GIVEN aFormIsPrescribed IS A BOOLEAN, theFormUsedIsInOrToTheLikeEffect IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s53 the form used is sufficient in law` MEANS
    IF aFormIsPrescribed AND theFormUsedIsInOrToTheLikeEffect AND (NOT contraryIntentionAppears) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 54 Construction of references to Acts`

DECLARE VicCopyOfAnImperialActReferredTo IS ONE OF
    VicTheRevisedEditionOfTheStatutesPrintedByAuthority                                    -- s 54(1)(a)
    VicTheEditionPreparedUnderTheDirectionOfTheRecordCommission                            -- s 54(1)(b)
    VicACopyPrintedByTheKingsPrinterOrUnderTheAuthorityOfHisMajestysStationeryOffice       -- s 54(1)(c)

-- s 54(1): unless the contrary intention appears, a reference to an Imperial Act is a reference (a) for Acts included in a revised edition of the statutes printed by authority, to that edition;
-- (b) for Acts not so included but included in the edition prepared under the direction of the Record Commission, to that edition; (c) in any other case, to a copy printed by the King's Printer or under the superintendence or authority of His Majesty's Stationery Office.
-- src:1092 | (1) A reference in an Act or subordinate instrument to an Imperial Act shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be construed as a reference—
-- src:1093 | (a) in the case of Acts included in any revised edition of the statutes printed by authority, to that edition;
-- src:1094 | (b) in the case of Acts not so included but included in the edition prepared under the direction of the Record Commission, to that edition; and
-- src:1096 | (c) in any other case, to a copy of the Act printed by the King's Printer or under the superintendence or authority of His Majesty's Stationery Office.
@ref s 54(1) (src:1092-1096)
GIVEN includedInARevisedEditionPrintedByAuthority IS A BOOLEAN, includedInTheRecordCommissionEdition IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE VicCopyOfAnImperialActReferredTo
`s54(1) the copy of the Imperial Act the reference points at` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN NOTHING
        IF includedInARevisedEditionPrintedByAuthority THEN JUST VicTheRevisedEditionOfTheStatutesPrintedByAuthority
        IF includedInTheRecordCommissionEdition THEN JUST VicTheEditionPreparedUnderTheDirectionOfTheRecordCommission
        OTHERWISE JUST VicACopyPrintedByTheKingsPrinterOrUnderTheAuthorityOfHisMajestysStationeryOffice

-- s 54(2): unless the contrary intention appears, a reference to an Act of an Australasian State is a reference to a copy of the Act printed by the government printer of that State.
-- src:1097 | (2) A reference in an Act or subordinate instrument to an Act of an Australasian State shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be construed as a reference to a copy of the Act printed by the government printer of that Australasian State.
@ref s 54(2) (src:1097)
GIVEN isAReferenceToAnActOfAnAustralasianState IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s54(2) the reference is a reference to a copy printed by the government printer of that State` MEANS
    IF isAReferenceToAnActOfAnAustralasianState AND (NOT contraryIntentionAppears) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE VicPrinterOfADocument IS ONE OF
    VicGovernmentPrinterOfAnAustralasianState
    VicGovernmentPrinterForVictoria
    VicGovernmentPrinterOfAnAustralasianStateOtherThanVictoria
    VicSomeOtherPrinter

-- s 54(2A): a document, whether made before, on or after the commencement of the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994, purporting to be a copy of an Act or subordinate instrument printed by the government printer of any Australasian State is on the mere production of that document admissible as evidence thereof before all courts and persons acting judicially within Victoria.
-- src:1099 | (2A) A document, whether made before, on or after the commencement of the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994, purporting to be a copy of an Act or subordinate instrument printed by the government printer of any Australasian State is on the mere production of that document admissible as evidence thereof before all courts and persons acting judicially within Victoria.
@ref s 54(2A) (src:1099)
GIVEN purportsToBeACopyOfAnActOrSubordinateInstrument IS A BOOLEAN, printer IS A VicPrinterOfADocument
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s54(2A) the document is admissible on its mere production` MEANS
    IF purportsToBeACopyOfAnActOrSubordinateInstrument AND (printer EQUALS VicGovernmentPrinterOfAnAustralasianState OR printer EQUALS VicGovernmentPrinterForVictoria OR printer EQUALS VicGovernmentPrinterOfAnAustralasianStateOtherThanVictoria)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 54(2B): a document made after the commencement of section 28 of the Miscellaneous Acts (Omnibus Amendments) Act 1995 purporting to be a copy of a reprint of an Act or a statutory rule printed by the Government Printer for Victoria is on the mere production admissible as evidence thereof.
-- The day that section 28 commenced is not in the text; whether the document was made after it is asked as an input.
-- src:1101 | (2B) A document made after the commencement of section 28 of the Miscellaneous Acts (Omnibus Amendments) Act 1995 purporting to be a copy of a reprint of an Act or a statutory rule printed by the Government Printer for Victoria is on the mere production of that document admissible as evidence thereof before all courts and persons acting judicially within Victoria.
@ref s 54(2B) (src:1101)
GIVEN purportsToBeACopyOfAReprintOfAnActOrStatutoryRule IS A BOOLEAN, printer IS A VicPrinterOfADocument, madeAfterTheCommencementOfSection28OfThe1995Act IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s54(2B) the document is admissible on its mere production` MEANS
    IF purportsToBeACopyOfAReprintOfAnActOrStatutoryRule AND printer EQUALS VicGovernmentPrinterForVictoria AND madeAfterTheCommencementOfSection28OfThe1995Act
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 54(2C): a document, whether made before, on or after that commencement, purporting to be a copy of a reprint of an Act or a statutory rule printed by the Government Printer of any Australasian State other than Victoria is, if the law of that State includes a provision corresponding to subsection (2B), on the mere production admissible as evidence thereof.
-- src:1103 | (2C) A document, whether made before, on or after the commencement of section 28 of the Miscellaneous Acts (Omnibus Amendments) Act 1995, purporting to be a copy of a reprint of an Act or a statutory rule printed by the Government Printer of any Australasian State (other than Victoria) is, if the law of that State includes a provision corresponding to subsection (2B) of this section, on the mere production of that document admissible as evidence thereof before all courts and persons acting judicially within Victoria.
@ref s 54(2C) (src:1103)
GIVEN purportsToBeACopyOfAReprintOfAnActOrStatutoryRule IS A BOOLEAN, printer IS A VicPrinterOfADocument, theLawOfThatStateIncludesAProvisionCorrespondingToSubsection2B IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s54(2C) the document is admissible on its mere production` MEANS
    IF purportsToBeACopyOfAReprintOfAnActOrStatutoryRule AND printer EQUALS VicGovernmentPrinterOfAnAustralasianStateOtherThanVictoria
    THEN (IF theLawOfThatStateIncludesAProvisionCorrespondingToSubsection2B THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 54(3): in this section the expressions Act, Australasian State and government printer have the same meanings as they have respectively in Divisions 4 and 6 of Part III of the Evidence (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act 1958.
-- That Act is not among the sources; the function says where the meaning is found.
-- src:1105 | (3) In this section the expressions Act, Australasian State and government printer have the same meanings as they have respectively in Divisions 4 and 6 of Part III of the Evidence (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act 1958.
@ref s 54(3) (src:1105)
GIVEN expression IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s54(3) where the meaning of the expression is found` MEANS
    IF expression EQUALS "Act" OR expression EQUALS "Australasian State" OR expression EQUALS "government printer"
    THEN JUST "Divisions 4 and 6 of Part III of the Evidence (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act 1958"
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 54A Style changes`

-- s 54A(2): the Chief Parliamentary Counsel, in preparing an Act or statutory rule for reprinting or other publication, may authorise an alteration to text or other matter forming part of it to give effect to the style changes set out in Schedule 1.
-- src:1109 | (1) Schedule 1 sets out style changes in Acts and statutory rules.
-- src:1110 | (2) The Chief Parliamentary Counsel, in preparing an Act or statutory rule for reprinting or other publication, may authorise an alteration to be made to text or other matter forming part of the Act or statutory rule to give effect to the style changes set out in Schedule 1.
@ref s 54A(1) and s 54A(2) (src:1109-1110)
GIVEN isInPreparingAnActOrStatutoryRuleForReprintingOrOtherPublication IS A BOOLEAN, givesEffectToAStyleChangeInSchedule1 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s54A(2) the Chief Parliamentary Counsel may authorise the alteration` MEANS
    IF isInPreparingAnActOrStatutoryRuleForReprintingOrOtherPublication AND givesEffectToAStyleChangeInSchedule1 THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE VicPurposeOfAnAlteration IS ONE OF
    VicSection21A_2OfThisAct
    VicSection18_2OfTheSubordinateLegislationAct1994
    VicAnyOtherPurposeOfTheAlteration

-- s 54A(3): an alteration made to an Act under subsection (2) has effect for all purposes, other than section 21A(2) of this Act, as if it had been made by an Act.
-- src:1111 | (3) An alteration made to an Act under subsection (2) has effect for all purposes, other than section 21A(2) of this Act, as if it had been made by an Act.
@ref s 54A(3) (src:1111)
GIVEN madeUnderSubsection2 IS A BOOLEAN, purpose IS A VicPurposeOfAnAlteration
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s54A(3) the alteration to an Act has effect for the purpose as if it had been made by an Act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT madeUnderSubsection2 THEN JUST FALSE
        IF purpose EQUALS VicSection21A_2OfThisAct THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 54A(4): an alteration made to a statutory rule under subsection (2) has effect for all purposes, other than section 18(2) of the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994, as if it had been made by a statutory rule.
-- src:1112 | (4) An alteration made to a statutory rule under subsection (2) has effect for all purposes, other than section 18(2) of the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994, as if it had been made by a statutory rule.
@ref s 54A(4) (src:1112)
GIVEN madeUnderSubsection2 IS A BOOLEAN, purpose IS A VicPurposeOfAnAlteration
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s54A(4) the alteration to a statutory rule has effect for the purpose as if it had been made by a statutory rule` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT madeUnderSubsection2 THEN JUST FALSE
        IF purpose EQUALS VicSection18_2OfTheSubordinateLegislationAct1994 THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 55 Construction of references to British subjects etc.`

DECLARE VicKindOfLawOfVictoria IS ONE OF
    VicAnActAsALawOfVictoria                                         -- s 55(1)(b)(i)
    VicASubordinateInstrumentAsALawOfVictoria                        -- s 55(1)(b)(ii)
    VicAnInstrumentHavingEffectByVirtueOfASubordinateInstrument      -- s 55(1)(b)(iii)
    VicNotALawOfVictoria

-- s 55(1)(b): law of Victoria means an Act, a subordinate instrument, and an instrument having effect by virtue of a subordinate instrument.
-- src:1118 | (b) law of Victoria means—
-- src:1119 | (i) an Act;
-- src:1120 | (ii) a subordinate instrument; and
-- src:1121 | (iii) an instrument having effect by virtue of a subordinate instrument.
@ref s 55(1)(b) (src:1118-1121)
GIVEN kind IS A VicKindOfLawOfVictoria
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s55(1)(b) the thing is a law of Victoria` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN VicNotALawOfVictoria THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 55(2)(a): the person's name was, at any time within the three months immediately before 26 January 1984, enrolled on a roll of the kinds named in (i) or (ii).
-- The three months run from the first day of the three calendar months ending immediately before 26 January 1984 (s 44(6)(b)) to the day before 26 January 1984.
-- src:1124 | (a) whose name was, at any time within the three months immediately before 26 January 1984, enrolled on—
-- src:1125 | (i) an electoral roll for an electoral district of the Legislative Assembly; or
-- src:1126 | (ii) an electoral roll maintained under any one of the Commonwealth Acts known as the Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918, the Australian Capital Territory Representation (House of Representatives) Act 1973 and the Northern Territory Representation Act 1922; or—
@ref s 55(2)(a) (src:1124-1126)
GIVEN dayNameWasEnrolled IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s55(2)(a) the name was enrolled on the day within the three months immediately before 26 January 1984` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s44(6)(b) first day of n calendar months ending immediately before a day` `s55(2)(a) day before which the three months are counted` 3
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST firstDay THEN JUST ((dayNameWasEnrolled AT LEAST firstDay) AND (dayNameWasEnrolled LESS THAN `s55(2)(a) day before which the three months are counted`))

-- s 55(2): a reference in any law of Victoria to a British subject, or a natural-born or naturalised subject of His Majesty, or any similar expression, is a reference to an Australian citizen or any other person within paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d).
-- Paragraphs (b) and (c) name a person who had not attained 18 before 26 January 1984 but whose name could have been enrolled at any such time if the person had attained that age (c: but for the operation of section 48(2) of the Constitution Act 1975).
-- Paragraph (d) names a person whose name could have been enrolled at any such time but before the operation of section 48(2) of the Constitution Act 1975.
-- The Constitution Act 1975 and the rolls are not among the sources: whether a name could have been enrolled is asked as an input.
-- src:1123 | (2) A reference in any law of Victoria to a British subject or to a natural-born or naturalised subject of His Majesty or to any other similar expression shall be construed as a reference to an Australian citizen or any other person—
-- src:1124 | (a) whose name was, at any time within the three months immediately before 26 January 1984, enrolled on—
-- src:1125 | (i) an electoral roll for an electoral district of the Legislative Assembly; or
-- src:1126 | (ii) an electoral roll maintained under any one of the Commonwealth Acts known as the Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918, the Australian Capital Territory Representation (House of Representatives) Act 1973 and the Northern Territory Representation Act 1922; or—
-- src:1127 | (b) who had not attained the full age of 18 years before that date but whose name could have been so enrolled at any such time if the person had attained that age before that date; or
-- src:1128 | (c) who had not attained the full age of 18 years before that date but whose name could have been so enrolled at any such time but for the operation of section 48(2) of the Constitution Act 1975 if the person had attained that age before that date; or
-- src:1129 | (d) whose name could have been so enrolled at any such time but before the operation of section 48(2) of the Constitution Act 1975.
@ref s 55(2) (src:1123-1129)
GIVEN isAnAustralianCitizen IS A BOOLEAN, withinParagraphA IS A BOOLEAN, withinParagraphB IS A BOOLEAN, couldHaveBeenEnrolledButForSection48_2 IS A BOOLEAN, notAttained18BeforeThatDate IS A BOOLEAN, couldHaveBeenEnrolledBeforeTheOperationOfSection48_2 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s55(2) the person is one to whom a reference to a British subject is construed as referring` MEANS
    IF isAnAustralianCitizen OR withinParagraphA OR withinParagraphB OR (notAttained18BeforeThatDate AND couldHaveBeenEnrolledButForSection48_2) OR couldHaveBeenEnrolledBeforeTheOperationOfSection48_2
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 55(3): where a rule of law applies to or has effect with respect to a British subject, it applies to an Australian citizen and a person to whom subsection (2)(a), (b), (c) or (d) applies as if that citizen or person were a British subject.
-- src:1131 | (3) Where a rule of law applies to or in relation to or has effect with respect to a British subject, that rule of law shall apply to or in relation to or shall have effect with respect to an Australian citizen and a person to whom subsection (2)(a), (b), (c) or (d) applies as if that Australian citizen or person were a British subject.
@ref s 55(3) (src:1131)
GIVEN ruleOfLawAppliesToABritishSubject IS A BOOLEAN, isAnAustralianCitizenOrAPersonToWhomSubsection2Applies IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s55(3) the rule of law applies to the person as if the person were a British subject` MEANS
    IF ruleOfLawAppliesToABritishSubject AND isAnAustralianCitizenOrAPersonToWhomSubsection2Applies THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 56 Construction of provisions relating to bankrupt or insolvent members of public bodies`

-- s 56: where an Act or subordinate instrument provides that a person who is or becomes bankrupt or insolvent shall not be capable of holding or continuing to hold the office of member of a municipal council or other public statutory body,
-- that incapacity shall extend to any person whose property is or becomes subject to control under the law relating to bankruptcy.
-- src:1135 | 56 Construction of provisions relating to bankrupt or insolvent members of public bodies
-- src:1136 | Where in an Act or subordinate instrument it is provided that a person who is or becomes bankrupt or is or becomes insolvent shall not be capable of holding or continuing to hold the office of member of a municipal council or other public statutory body, that incapacity shall extend to any person whose property is or becomes subject to control under the law relating to bankruptcy.
@ref s 56 (src:1135-1136)
GIVEN theActOrInstrumentProvidesThatABankruptOrInsolventPersonIsIncapableOfBeingAMemberOfAPublicBody IS A BOOLEAN, propertyIsOrBecomesSubjectToControlUnderTheLawRelatingToBankruptcy IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s56 the incapacity extends to the person` MEANS
    IF theActOrInstrumentProvidesThatABankruptOrInsolventPersonIsIncapableOfBeingAMemberOfAPublicBody AND propertyIsOrBecomesSubjectToControlUnderTheLawRelatingToBankruptcy
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 57 Application of laws of Victoria in certain off-shore areas`

DECLARE VicKindOfLawForS57 IS ONE OF
    VicALawOfTheCommonwealth                                                 -- s 57(3)(a)
    VicACriminalLawOfTheStateAsToTheOffshoreAreaItsSeaBedSubsoilOrAirspace   -- s 57(3)(b)
    VicACriminalLawOfTheStateAsToTheCoastalWatersOfVictoriaOrTheirSeaBedSubsoilOrAirspace   -- s 57(3)(c)
    VicAnyOtherLawInForceInVictoria

-- s 57(1) and (3): subject to the section, the laws in force in Victoria (written or unwritten, as in force from time to time) and any instrument made under them apply in the offshore area;
-- the section does not operate to apply Commonwealth law, or the criminal laws of the State in or in relation to the offshore area or the coastal waters of Victoria or the sea-bed, subsoil or airspace.
-- src:1140 | (1) Subject to this section, the provisions of the laws in force in Victoria whether written or unwritten and as in force from time to time and the provisions of any instrument made under any of those laws apply in the offshore area.
-- src:1150 | (3) This section does not operate—
-- src:1152 | (a) to apply in the offshore area the provisions of any law of the Commonwealth; or
-- src:1154 | (b) to apply the provisions of the criminal laws of the State to or in relation to the offshore area or the sea-bed or subsoil beneath or the airspace above that offshore area; or
-- src:1156 | (c) to apply the provisions of the criminal laws of the State to or in relation to the coastal waters of Victoria or the sea-bed or subsoil beneath or the airspace above those waters.
@ref s 57(1) and s 57(3) (src:1140-1156)
GIVEN kind IS A VicKindOfLawForS57
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s57(1),(3) the law applies in the offshore area by force of s 57` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN VicALawOfTheCommonwealth THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN VicACriminalLawOfTheStateAsToTheOffshoreAreaItsSeaBedSubsoilOrAirspace THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN VicACriminalLawOfTheStateAsToTheCoastalWatersOfVictoriaOrTheirSeaBedSubsoilOrAirspace THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN VicAnyOtherLawInForceInVictoria THEN JUST TRUE

-- s 57(2): the provisions apply to and in relation to (a) any act done or omitted at a place in the offshore area within the outer limits of the coastal waters of Victoria; (b) any act done or omitted in the offshore area by a person connected with Victoria;
-- (c) any matter, thing or circumstance existing or arising in the offshore area which involves or relates to persons connected with Victoria; as if the offshore area were part of Victoria.
-- src:1142 | (2) The provisions referred to in subsection (1) apply to and in relation to—
-- src:1144 | (a) any act done or omitted to be done at a place in the offshore area which is within the outer limits of the coastal waters of Victoria;
-- src:1146 | (b) any act done or omitted to be done in the offshore area by a person connected with Victoria; and
-- src:1148 | (c) any matter, thing or circumstance existing or arising in the offshore area which involves or relates to persons connected with Victoria—
-- src:1149 | as if the offshore area were part of Victoria.
@ref s 57(2) (src:1142-1149)
GIVEN doneOrOmittedAtAPlaceInTheOffshoreAreaWithinTheOuterLimitsOfTheCoastalWaters IS A BOOLEAN, doneOrOmittedInTheOffshoreAreaByAPersonConnectedWithVictoria IS A BOOLEAN, aMatterInTheOffshoreAreaInvolvingOrRelatingToPersonsConnectedWithVictoria IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s57(2) the provisions apply as if the offshore area were part of Victoria` MEANS
    IF doneOrOmittedAtAPlaceInTheOffshoreAreaWithinTheOuterLimitsOfTheCoastalWaters OR doneOrOmittedInTheOffshoreAreaByAPersonConnectedWithVictoria OR aMatterInTheOffshoreAreaInvolvingOrRelatingToPersonsConnectedWithVictoria
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 57(4): subject to the section, the several courts of Victoria are invested with jurisdiction in all matters arising under the provisions of the laws applied by the section.
-- src:1157 | (4) Subject to this section, the several courts of Victoria are invested with jurisdiction in all matters arising under the provisions of the laws applied by this section.
@ref s 57(4) (src:1157)
GIVEN theMatterArisesUnderALawAppliedByS57 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s57(4) the courts of Victoria have jurisdiction in the matter` MEANS
    IF theMatterArisesUnderALawAppliedByS57 THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE VicWeightOfAnAverment IS ONE OF
    VicEvidenceOnly
    VicConclusiveEvidence

-- s 57(5): for the purposes of proceedings for an offence against the law of Victoria, an averment in an indictment, charge-sheet or complaint that a person was at a specified time or period a person connected with Victoria is evidence and, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, conclusive evidence of the fact averred.
-- src:1159 | (5) For the purposes of proceedings for an offence against the law of Victoria an averment in an indictment, charge-sheet or complaint that—
-- src:1160 | (a) a person was at a specified time or in respect of a specified period a person connected with Victoria—
-- src:1163 | shall be evidence and, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, conclusive evidence of the fact averred.
@ref s 57(5) (src:1159-1163)
GIVEN isAnAverment IS A BOOLEAN, inProceedingsForAnOffenceAgainstTheLawOfVictoria IS A BOOLEAN, thereIsEvidenceToTheContrary IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE VicWeightOfAnAverment
`s57(5) the weight of the averment that a person was a person connected with Victoria` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (isAnAverment AND inProceedingsForAnOffenceAgainstTheLawOfVictoria) THEN NOTHING
        IF thereIsEvidenceToTheContrary THEN JUST VicEvidenceOnly
        OTHERWISE JUST VicConclusiveEvidence

-- s 57(6)(c): person connected with Victoria means a person who (i) is domiciled in Victoria; (ii) is permanently or temporarily resident in Victoria;
-- (iii) being a body corporate has a place of business in or carries on business in Victoria or is registered in or incorporated or established under a law of Victoria;
-- (iv) is on or operating from a ship, boat or vessel licensed or registered or required to be licensed or registered under a law of Victoria;
-- (v) is on or operating from a rig or other structure or installation in the adjacent area the operation or function of which is regulated by a law of the Commonwealth or of Victoria.
-- src:1175 | (c) person connected with Victoria means a person who—
-- src:1176 | (i) is domiciled in Victoria;
-- src:1177 | (ii) is permanently or temporarily resident in Victoria;
-- src:1178 | (iii) being a body corporate has a place of business in or carries on business in Victoria or is registered in or incorporated or established under a law of Victoria;
-- src:1179 | (iv) is on or is operating from a ship, boat or vessel of any kind licensed or registered or required to be licensed or registered under a law of Victoria; or
-- src:1180 | (v) is on or operating from a rig or other structure or installation of any kind in the adjacent area the operation or function of which is regulated by a law of the Commonwealth or of Victoria.
@ref s 57(6)(c) (src:1175-1180)
GIVEN isDomiciledInVictoria IS A BOOLEAN, isResidentInVictoria IS A BOOLEAN, isABodyCorporateWithAPlaceOfBusinessOrCarryingOnBusinessInVictoriaOrRegisteredOrEstablishedUnderALawOfVictoria IS A BOOLEAN, isOnOrOperatingFromAVesselLicensedOrRegisteredUnderALawOfVictoria IS A BOOLEAN, isOnOrOperatingFromARigOrStructureRegulatedByALawOfTheCommonwealthOrVictoria IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s57(6)(c) the person is a person connected with Victoria` MEANS
    JUST (isDomiciledInVictoria OR isResidentInVictoria OR isABodyCorporateWithAPlaceOfBusinessOrCarryingOnBusinessInVictoriaOrRegisteredOrEstablishedUnderALawOfVictoria OR isOnOrOperatingFromAVesselLicensedOrRegisteredUnderALawOfVictoria OR isOnOrOperatingFromARigOrStructureRegulatedByALawOfTheCommonwealthOrVictoria)

-- s 57(6)(a), (b), (ba), (bb), (bc): the other defined expressions; each is given by pointing at an Act of the Commonwealth or of Victoria, or by a description. The function says where each is found.
-- src:1166 | (a) offshore area means so much of the area described in item 2 of Schedule 1 to the Offshore Petroleum and Greenhouse Gas Storage Act 2006 of the Commonwealth in relation to Victoria as is within the outer limits of the continental shelf and includes the space above and below that area;
-- src:1168 | (b) coastal waters of Victoria has the same meaning as the expression coastal waters of the State has in relation to Victoria under the Coastal Waters (State Powers) Act 1980 of the Commonwealth;
-- src:1170 | (ba) cooperative scheme has the same meaning as that expression has in the Crimes at Sea Act 1999;
-- src:1172 | (bb) continental shelf has the same meaning as in the Seas and Submerged Lands Act 1973 (Commonwealth);
-- src:1174 | (bc) criminal laws means the substantive criminal law, and the law of criminal investigation, procedure and evidence, within the meaning of the cooperative scheme;
@ref s 57(6)(a) and s 57(6)(b) and s 57(6)(ba) and s 57(6)(bb) and s 57(6)(bc) (src:1166-1174)
GIVEN expression IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s57(6) where the meaning of the expression is found` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF expression EQUALS "offshore area" THEN JUST "item 2 of Schedule 1 to the Offshore Petroleum and Greenhouse Gas Storage Act 2006 of the Commonwealth, so much of the area as is within the outer limits of the continental shelf, including the space above and below"
        IF expression EQUALS "coastal waters of Victoria" THEN JUST "the Coastal Waters (State Powers) Act 1980 of the Commonwealth"
        IF expression EQUALS "cooperative scheme" THEN JUST "the Crimes at Sea Act 1999"
        IF expression EQUALS "continental shelf" THEN JUST "the Seas and Submerged Lands Act 1973 (Commonwealth)"
        IF expression EQUALS "criminal laws" THEN JUST "the substantive criminal law, and the law of criminal investigation, procedure and evidence, within the meaning of the cooperative scheme"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 58 Declaration of validity of certain laws`

-- s 58(1): each provision of an Act or subordinate instrument enacted or made, or purporting to have been, before the commencement of the Australia Acts has the same effect as it would have had, and is as effective as it would have been,
-- if the Australia Acts had been in operation at the time of its enactment or making, or purported enactment or making.
-- The day the Australia Acts commenced is not in the text; whether the provision was enacted or made before it is asked as an input.
-- src:1184 | (1) Each provision of an Act or subordinate instrument enacted or made, or purporting to have been enacted or made, before the commencement of the Australia Acts—
-- src:1185 | (a) has the same effect as it would have had; and
-- src:1186 | (b) is as valid as it would have been—
-- src:1187 | if the Australia Acts had been in operation at the time of its enactment or making, or purported enactment or making.
@ref s 58(1) (src:1184-1187)
GIVEN enactedOrMadeOrPurportedBeforeTheCommencementOfTheAustraliaActs IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s58(1) the provision has the same effect, and is as effective, as it would have been if the Australia Acts had been in operation` MEANS
    IF enactedOrMadeOrPurportedBeforeTheCommencementOfTheAustraliaActs THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- s 58(2): Australia Acts means the Australia Act 1986 of the Commonwealth and the Australia Act 1986 of the United Kingdom.
-- src:1188 | (2) In this section, Australia Acts means—
-- src:1189 | (a) the Australia Act 1986 of the Commonwealth; and
-- src:1190 | (b) the Australia Act 1986 of the United Kingdom.
@ref s 58(2) (src:1188-1190)
GIVEN thing IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s58(2) the thing is one of the Australia Acts` MEANS
    IF thing EQUALS "the Australia Act 1986 of the Commonwealth" OR thing EQUALS "the Australia Act 1986 of the United Kingdom" THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
